      {
        "id": 38610,
        "name": "logan_mann",
        "username": "logan_mann",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/43a26b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-18T14:42:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"TheJayMann\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/48/2261_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheJayMann:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I honestly don't see any reason why the flavor text from the core set would no longer be cannon.&nbsp; The gameplay functionality, yes, but not the flavor.&nbsp; The Enhanced Edition would simply contain more flavor text, not replacing the old.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I just wonder if from their side of things they discovered typos in the text that they realized they needed to change. We wouldn't know if a typo put something out of skew with the rest of the multiverse plot lines or not.</p>\n<p>But I certainly hope you are right…this back story element is one of my favorite things about the game.</p>",
