        "id": 38617,
        "name": "flamethrower49",
        "username": "flamethrower49",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-19T21:09:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"TheJayMann\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/48/2261_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheJayMann:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What he means, in the proofs, when you played the Staff of Ra, you regained 5 hp.&nbsp; In the released prints, you now regain 3 hp instead.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Ah, right.&nbsp; Well, it probably took just a couple game of playtesting to realize how crazy that was.&nbsp; I remember posting about gaining 25 life one game by continuously playing staves.&nbsp; So they changed it after posting the proofs, which I figured they would do&nbsp;with some things.&nbsp; Same with card counts.&nbsp; It's interesting, though.</p>",
